# Integer32 literal below the minimum

Verifies a negated int32 literal whose signed magnitude is below the 32-bit
minimum is rejected with a compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI
pipeline.

>>> source
const too_small: int32 = -2147483649
print(too_small)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `-2147483649` for type `int32`: number too small to fit in target type at Span { start: 25, end: 36 }

<<< exit
1
